From 333043bbd0170d3e6d51b546eee466e87dc9a561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:13:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Reuse recorded AutoFDO profiles at job time, honour
 Portage's signing key
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The newest recorded profile is picked up in prepare_build, after the
  wizard or --set has turned AutoFDO on, not only when the plan is created;
  loose *.afdo files dropped into the profiles directory count too.
- The build script uses an existing MODULES_SIGN_KEY/MODULES_SIGN_CERT from
  Portage when present, so a machine never ends up with two signing keys.
- The signing files are recorded under /var/lib/kernelsmith/portage/, where
  Library → "Runtime tuning & Portage" can remove them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
